{"title":"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with circumcentre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are interior points of the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9141cf60419b778a5a3a2d5c6ef4d5e5200ff45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/666a267ed622c158b00676df18f0fd043c8504e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP,CQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> be the circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9141cf60419b778a5a3a2d5c6ef4d5e5200ff45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is tangent to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e6b8eb3853536162118052909c13b675829f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=OQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p><i>Author: Sergei Berlov, Russia</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/c1zwoYCMR28\">https://youtu.be/c1zwoYCMR28</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e2ab80a07a1e3b2c6085f96ff2d9918f03420b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] dot(&quot;O&quot;, (50, 38), N); dot(&quot;A&quot;, (40, 100), N); dot(&quot;B&quot;, (0, 0), S); dot(&quot;C&quot;, (100, 0), S); dot(&quot;Q&quot;, (24, 60), W); dot(&quot;P&quot;, (52, 80), E); dot(&quot;L&quot;, (62, 30), SE); dot(&quot;M&quot;, (38, 70), N); dot(&quot;K&quot;, (27, 42), W); draw((100, 0)--(24, 60), dotted); draw((0, 0)--(52, 80), dashed); draw((0, 0)--(100, 0)--(40, 100)--cycle); draw((24, 60)--(52, 80)); draw((27, 42)--(38, 70)--(62, 30)--cycle); draw(circle((49, 49), 23)); label(&quot;$\\Gamma$&quot;, (72, 49), E); draw(circle((50, 38), 63)); label(&quot;$\\omega$&quot;, (-13, 38), NW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\nDiagram by qwertysri987\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>By parallel lines and the tangency condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/1365f528027535869e44078ab8b2617fff874219.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle APM\\cong \\angle LMP \\cong \\angle LKM.\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"13\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21d90488798387cebb7eed35bf3360df74a54d71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AQP\\cong \\angle KLM,\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" /> so AA similarity implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/17760a0f4f38356e1b8e5ebd37f90c199b297113.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle APQ\\sim \\triangle MKL.\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"17\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> denote the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8dcf98ed1b21dbc446aa28d097d4281599c25e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> its circumradius. As both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcdcd9c8cdbd7c4679fd83fca62a617ba3727fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87988879827bec3d9a546c801e4965d8fa44a94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} R^2-QO^2&amp;=\\text{Pow}_{\\omega}(Q)\\\\ &amp;=QB\\cdot AQ \\\\ &amp;=2AQ\\cdot MK\\\\ &amp;=2AP\\cdot ML\\\\ &amp;=AP\\cdot PC\\\\ &amp;=\\text{Pow}_{\\omega}(P)\\\\ &amp;=R^2-PO^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"190\" height=\"167\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de021266fe2a83dc9bce964b7281d86dbc77720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=OQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO\" title=\"2009 IMO\">2009 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221840\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 186/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2